## Step 3a (9/14/26): baseline 0DTE quotes -- `pull_baseline_quotes.py` (Zach runs it from Git Bash)

Goal: a "normalized baseline price of OTM options" per name so each event's strangle cost can be expressed as a
multiple of the name's own normal Friday. For every event, the 5 Fridays strictly before eff_date (rolled to the
prior trading day on holidays; MRVL's Thursday eff date still maps to Fridays) get the same pull as the event day:
0DTE chain, strikes within 8% of the 15:00 spot, 15:00-16:00 at 1s -> t_opra_quotes via pull_0dte_quotes.pull_pair.
Names without weeklies only have a chain on the monthly inside the window; other Fridays log `no_chain`.
Spot snaps 15:00/15:10/.../15:40 + PX_LAST per baseline day -> `baseline_spots.csv`; checkpoints ->
`_baseline_pull_meta.csv`. 19 events x 5 = 95 pairs; ~1 min per pair with a chain.
Next (3b): price the first-OTM strangle on each baseline day at each entry time, take the median cost_bps per
(symbol, entry) as the baseline, report event cost_bps / baseline.

## Step 2b (9/10/26): strangle backtest -- `backtest_strangle.py`

- Trade: at 15:00 buy the 0DTE call and put each >= 120 bps OTM vs the 15:00 CloudQuant spot (nearest such strike),
  fill = bid + 70% x spread, entry = median fill over 15:00:00-15:00:10, hold to expiry (intrinsic at PX_LAST).
  A zero bid is a real no-bid market (fill = 70% x ask), not a bad quote.
- Result (19 events, first pass): mean cost 31 bps (median 18), mean payoff 27 bps, mean pnl -4 bps, win rate 26%
  (5 of 19 finish ITM), Sharpe -0.12, payoff/cost 0.87. >= $10B bucket (13): pnl +0.4 bps/event, payoff/cost 1.01;
  $7-10B bucket (6): -14 bps/event, payoff/cost 0.35. Winners: CVNA +87, APP +70, MRVL +22, CRH +15, CRWD +8.
- Caveat: strike spacing makes the average leg ~165 bps OTM (not 120), and 0DTE vol varies hugely by name
  (MRVL strangle cost 192 bps, AAPL/DELL 6-7 bps) -- a fixed OTM distance is not a fixed budget.
- Knobs: `OTM_BPS`, `SPREAD_PAID`, `ENTRY_TIME`, `ENTRY_WINDOW_SEC`, `MIN_FLOW_BN`; `run_backtest()` takes them as args
  so entry-time / OTM sweeps are one loop over the cached quotes.

### Refinement 9/14/26 (Zach): cost cap + limit-order exit
- If the strangle costs > `MAX_COST_BPS` (120 bps) push both strikes out one strike (`MAX_PUSHES` = 1). Only MRVL
  triggers (192 -> 142 bps at 330/315, still above the cap after one push).
- Exit variant: resting sell limit on EACH leg at `LIMIT_MULT` (2x) the total strangle cost; a leg fills if its max
  bid after entry (cached 1-sec bars, one SQL query per event) reaches the limit, filled at the limit; unfilled legs
  expire at intrinsic. A single fill therefore returns +cost (100%) plus the other leg's intrinsic.
- Result (19 events): at least one leg hit 2x in 6 of 19 (AVGO, CVNA, APP, AAPL, CRWD, UBER; 46% of the >= $10B
  events), both legs only AAPL. Mean pnl -7 bps vs -5.6 hold: the cap costs more on CVNA (+87 -> +16) and APP
  (+70 -> +42) than it earns on the expire-worthless fills. Sum of max bids averages 2.4x cost (median 1.8x) and the
  max bids cluster 15:45-16:00, so the option value shows up late. Limit-multiple sweep 1.5x/2x/3x/4x: mean pnl
  -6.6 / -7.0 / -5.5 / -7.6 bps, any-leg fill 42% / 32% / 21% / 5% -- no multiple turns it positive.
- **Current default `LIMIT_MULT = 1.0` (Zach 9/14/26):** rest an offer at the TOTAL strangle cost in each leg (pay
  $1 + $1 -> $2 offers in both). One fill recoups the premium (pnl 0 + other leg's intrinsic); two fills = +cost.
  Result (19 events): mean +2.0 bps, median 0, win rate 21% (4 events: MRVL +142 both filled, AVGO +8, AAPL +7, CRH
  +15 unfilled put ITM), 12 of 19 got at least one fill, 3 got both. >= $10B bucket +6.2 bps/event (77% any fill,
  23% both); $7-10B -6.9 bps. Gives up CVNA (+87 -> 0) and APP (+70 -> 0) hold pnl; MRVL is 142 of the 38 total bps.
- Entry-time sweep (9/14/26, top-4 flows AAPL/MRVL/APP/AVGO, `sweep_entry_times()`, spot = CloudQuant snap at entry):
  limit-exit total 15:00 / 15:10 / 15:20 / 15:30 / 15:40 = +158 / +19 / +18 / +17 / +11 bps -- the 15:00 edge is
  MRVL's double fill (+142); from 15:10 on only its put fills (0). AVGO fills both legs at every entry (+8 to +12),
  APP only ever fills the call (0), AAPL fills both through 15:30 (+5 to +8) and at 15:40 only the put (0, hold +66).
  Hold-to-close improves with later entry (mean +12 -> +71 bps; MRVL strangle cost falls 142 -> 86 bps while the
  close move is fixed) but that is the same 4 names, not a new signal.
- 15:40 entry, hold to expiry, all 19 (9/14/26): total +147 bps, mean +7.8, median loss, win 32% (6 of 19), Sharpe
  0.13, payoff/cost 1.30, mean cost 25 bps. >= $10B: +151 total / +11.6 mean / 38% win; $7-10B: -4 total. MRVL is
  +200 of the +147 (strangle 86 bps vs 555 bps move); ex-MRVL -53. Other winners CRH +88, AAPL +66, APP +30, CVNA +27,
  UBER +5. Strikes re-picked off the 15:40 spot (AAPL 237.5/230, MRVL 337.5/320 after one push).
